  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of essential lifesaving GBV response services to women and girls affected by the earthquake in Aleppo, Hama, and Latakia governorates</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNFPA proposes to provide gender-based violence (GBV) response and risk mitigation services to earthquake-affected populations to prevent the negative consequences of GBV and mitigate further risks in Jebel Saman, Hama, Jablah districts of Aleppo, Hama and Latakia governorates respectively. This will be accomplished by ensuring availability of access to and utilization of comprehensive, lifesaving GBV response services by establishing temporary Women and Girls&#x2019; Safe Spaces in areas closer to the collective shelters which are identified by the government to be mid-term shelters for the displaced people. In addition, UNFPA proposes to train specialized GBV service providers on GBV basics, case management and PSEA models, to ensure quality service delivery and mitigate the risks of potential harm to affected people.</narrative>
  </description>
